eux officials <ei28 said> last week that they are \" highly confident \" the offer will be <ei30 approved> once it <ei31 submits> details of its proposed investments to federal regulators . Both offers are conditional on regulatory approvals and enough shares being tendered to give the bidders a majority of Connaught 's shares outstanding . Institut Merieux , which already holds a 12.5 % stake in Connaught , <ei32 said> that at the <ei33 close> of business Thursday , 5,745,188 shares of Connaught and C $ 44.3 million face amount of debentures , convertible into 1,826,596 common shares , had been <ei35 tendered> to its <ei36 offer> . At the <ei37 close> of business Thursday , Ciba - Geigy and Chiron <ei39 said> 11,580 common shares had been <ei40 tendered> to their <ei41 offer> . At last <ei42 report> , Connaught <ei43 had> 21.8 million shares outstanding . Separately , the Ontario Supreme Court <ei44 said> it will <ei45 postpone> indefinitely a <ei46 ruling> on the lawsuit <ei47 launched> by the University of Toronto against Connaught in connection with the Merieux bid . In a statement prepared by lawyers for the university and Connaught , the parties <ei48 said> they <ei49 agreed> that as a result of <ei51 reaching> a C415 million research accord , \" It is <ei52 unnecessary> that there be a judgment on the merits { of the case } at this time . \" Lawyers for the two sides were n't immediately available for comment . The university had <ei53 sought> an <ei54 injunction> blocking Connaught 's board from <ei55 recommending> or <ei56 supporting> an <ei57 offer> for the company by Merieux .", "gold": [["ei51", "causes", "ei52"], ["ei54", "causes", "ei55"], ["ei54", "causes", "ei56"], ["ei52", "causedby", "ei51"], ["ei55", "causedby", "ei54"], ["ei56", "causedby", "ei54"]], "lang": "eng", "mentions": ["ei1", "ei2", "ei3", "ei5", "ei6", "ei7", "ei8", "ei9", "ei12", "ei13", "ei15", "ei17", "ei18", "ei19", "ei20", "ei21", "ei22", "ei23", "ei24", "ei25", "ei27", "ei28", "ei